 \subsection{Introduction}\label{scale-introduction}
 
 Two working disciplines govern the exact treatment of belief-state safety values: evaluate exactly where you probe, and store the antichain of maximal survivable sets rather than the lattice (Abaee, 2026, An obstruction calculus). This paper asks whether the exact discipline survives the curse of dimensionality, and what new structure appears there. On the instance studied here the answer is affirmative, and the structure changes: the four-parameter cube is not a larger version of the two-parameter instance but a different regime. The cube is the paper's running instance; every structural claim below is instantiated on it.
